{"authored" [{"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=-1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(4-\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{4-\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c\\text{ }⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-1-\\text{i}})+5 \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (-1+\\text{i})+5 \\\\  & =-5+3\\text{i}+5 \\\\  & =3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b9aea95bc2b0f3d0948763302c4c26ff7579af434895f23f3da082a34876c014" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5+3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,-ia⟩=-i⟨a,a⟩$ for any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  By the antilinearity of $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$  in the second argument we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ia⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\ne -i⟨a,a⟩\n$$\n\n \nfor any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}.$\n\n- Statement II  is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ba819197e62679466ab9978e946d3b0c5575742504b572d13113662cc19999a" "basis" 1828 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-97186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=1+\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(3+2\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{3+2\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}+\\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot (-2\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4(-1)+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-3-7\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "82795b2335fa4e93428dcb8f3fd4318fb308a7d85fe4917b9dd19eb0df0f46e8"} {"question" "q-97186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2-\\text{i}"] ["math" "-3-7\\text{i}"] ["math" "-4\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\text{i}"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3-7\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=-1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(4-\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{4-\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c\\text{ }⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-1-\\text{i}})+5 \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (-1+\\text{i})+5 \\\\  & =-5+3\\text{i}+5 \\\\  & =3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "82795b2335fa4e93428dcb8f3fd4318fb308a7d85fe4917b9dd19eb0df0f46e8"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "-5+3\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\text{i}"] ["math" "3\\text{i}"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "82795b2335fa4e93428dcb8f3fd4318fb308a7d85fe4917b9dd19eb0df0f46e8"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,0⟩=0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $2⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the antilinearity in the second argument we have that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,0⟩ & =⟨a,0\\cdot 0⟩=\\overset{―}{0}⟨a,0⟩=0⟨a,0⟩=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,-2b⟩=\\overset{―}{(-2)}⟨a,b⟩=-2⟨a,b⟩\\ne 2⟨a,b⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063417/state.json" "file_sha256" "847d782a74163011f99012ce0abe0011239e24782c02c19f0787686ad7584fbf"} {"question" "q-97305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :quest